1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,520
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:04,670
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:05,770
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:08,370
I've been framing houses
for thirty years.

5
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:09,530
Up and down ladders,

6
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:10,410
kneeling on the deck,

7
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:12,290
nailing walls together all
day.

8
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:13,420
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,870
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:16,850
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:18,300
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:19,880
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:20,880
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:21,970
This is different.

15
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:22,560
Tight.

16
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:23,090
Full.

17
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:24,010
Like a band around

18
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:25,690
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,070
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:28,520
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,520
Give it time.

22
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,810
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:33,180
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,430
At three months,

25
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:35,500
give it six.

26
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:36,700
At six months,

27
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,340
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:39,340
At a year,

29
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,330
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:42,800
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:44,190
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:45,760
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:46,680
Every session,

34
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,260
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,430 --> 00:00:49,580
I got stronger.

36
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:50,930
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:52,430
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:53,760
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:56,010
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,010 --> 00:00:57,020
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:58,260
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:00,070
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:01,950
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:01,990 --> 00:01:03,260
And after that, a second

45
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:04,370
operation to go back

46
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:05,660
in and do it over.

47
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:06,790
I said no.

48
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:08,720
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:09,750
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:11,400
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,800
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,510
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:17,020
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,630
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:18,630 --> 00:01:19,840
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:21,500
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:23,040
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

58
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:25,320
game without shifting
every two minutes.

59
00:01:25,430 --> 00:01:26,470
On the job,

60
00:01:26,470 --> 00:01:28,310
the younger guys on my
crew started

61
00:01:28,310 --> 00:01:29,900
carrying my lumber for me.

62
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,390
Nobody said anything.

63
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:32,850
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:34,770
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:34,770 --> 00:01:36,160
like getting in the truck

66
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,630
or up off the couch,

67
00:01:37,630 --> 00:01:38,710
into a decision.

68
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,440
After a long and serious

69
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,750
talk with my wife,

70
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:43,580
I went back in one more
time.

71
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:45,060
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:46,690
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,890
And like the three before
it,

74
00:01:48,890 --> 00:01:51,870
the answer was everything
looks great.

75
00:01:51,910 --> 00:01:53,870
No loosening, no
infection,

76
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:54,750
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:56,400
Only this time

78
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,840
there was no new number.

79
00:01:57,880 --> 00:02:00,330
Nobody said give it
another six months.

80
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,330
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,720
I sat in the parking

82
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:04,790
lot for a while.

83
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:06,260
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:08,430
Then explain this.

85
00:02:08,507 --> 00:02:10,637
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

86
00:02:10,637 --> 00:02:12,067
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:12,167 --> 00:02:13,957
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:14,037 --> 00:02:15,207
I had walls to stand

89
00:02:15,207 --> 00:02:16,057
up at seven.

90
00:02:16,397 --> 00:02:18,267
Everyone in the house was
asleep

91
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:19,967
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

92
00:02:19,967 --> 00:02:21,197
with my leg up,

93
00:02:21,197 --> 00:02:23,127
trying to find any angle
where

94
00:02:23,127 --> 00:02:24,267
it didn't feel like
something

95
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:26,437
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

96
00:02:26,687 --> 00:02:29,157
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

97
00:02:29,397 --> 00:02:31,167
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

98
00:02:31,507 --> 00:02:32,267
And I just thought,

99
00:02:32,267 --> 00:02:33,957
is this really my life
now?

100
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:35,767
I can't live like this.

101
00:02:35,927 --> 00:02:37,567
Thirty years of framing,

102
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:38,667
and I didn't know how many
more

103
00:02:38,667 --> 00:02:39,967
houses I had in me.

104
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:41,927
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:42,017 --> 00:02:42,937
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:42,937 --> 00:02:44,347
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:44,587 --> 00:02:45,827
And when I found one,

108
00:02:45,827 --> 00:02:46,937
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:46,937 --> 00:02:48,247
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:48,357 --> 00:02:49,447
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:49,447 --> 00:02:50,867
out and went looking.

112
00:02:51,057 --> 00:02:52,307
Not for a product.

113
00:02:52,347 --> 00:02:53,547
For an explanation.

114
00:02:53,837 --> 00:02:55,577
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:55,577 --> 00:02:57,607
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:57,607 --> 00:02:58,917
doctor videos,

117
00:02:58,917 --> 00:03:00,277
medical animations.

118
00:03:00,497 --> 00:03:01,917
And that's when I found a
video

119
00:03:01,917 --> 00:03:03,637
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

120
00:03:03,677 --> 00:03:05,047
Steven Salinger,

121
00:03:05,047 --> 00:03:06,247
whose own wife had been

122
00:03:06,247 --> 00:03:07,597
through exactly this.

123
00:03:07,747 --> 00:03:09,507
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:09,507 --> 00:03:10,977
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:11,257 --> 00:03:13,237
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:13,277 --> 00:03:14,167
The ice.

127
00:03:14,227 --> 00:03:16,017
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:16,097 --> 00:03:17,577
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:17,617 --> 00:03:18,987
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:19,077 --> 00:03:21,047
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:21,217 --> 00:03:23,227
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:23,397 --> 00:03:24,427
It's a preview.

133
00:03:24,907 --> 00:03:25,847
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:25,847 --> 00:03:27,117
you this works fast.

135
00:03:27,157 --> 00:03:28,037
It doesn't.

136
00:03:28,437 --> 00:03:30,257
But if you're willing to
be patient,

137
00:03:30,257 --> 00:03:31,077
and to look at what's

138
00:03:31,077 --> 00:03:32,417
going on around your new
knee

139
00:03:32,417 --> 00:03:33,987
instead of inside it,
there

140
00:03:33,987 --> 00:03:36,147
is a real reason it still
hurts.

141
00:03:36,237 --> 00:03:37,947
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:38,207 --> 00:03:39,447
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:39,447 --> 00:03:41,487
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:41,487 --> 00:03:42,667
everything for me.

145
00:03:42,817 --> 00:03:44,487
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:44,637 --> 00:03:46,007
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:46,007 --> 00:03:47,517
the worn joint surfaces

148
00:03:47,517 --> 00:03:49,407
and puts in metal and
plastic.

149
00:03:49,557 --> 00:03:51,297
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:51,297 --> 00:03:52,787
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:53,007 --> 00:03:54,267
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:55,977
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:55,977 --> 00:03:57,377
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:03:57,557 --> 00:03:58,317
He said,

155
00:03:58,317 --> 00:03:59,577
think about a swollen foot

156
00:03:59,577 --> 00:04:00,677
inside a shoe.

157
00:04:00,927 --> 00:04:02,277
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:02,507 --> 00:04:04,577
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:07,077
so everything feels
cramped and tight

160
00:04:07,077 --> 00:04:08,247
and squeezed.

161
00:04:08,347 --> 00:04:09,377
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:09,377 --> 00:04:10,757
in a limited space

163
00:04:10,757 --> 00:04:13,107
with living tissue packed
all around it.

164
00:04:13,287 --> 00:04:15,227
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:15,227 --> 00:04:16,937
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:17,187 --> 00:04:20,107
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:20,237 --> 00:04:21,677
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:22,037 --> 00:04:23,737
But in some people that
swelling can

169
00:04:23,737 --> 00:04:26,327
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

170
00:04:26,517 --> 00:04:28,177
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:28,177 --> 00:04:29,957
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:30,067 --> 00:04:32,077
So when you bend,

173
00:04:32,077 --> 00:04:33,997
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:34,177 --> 00:04:35,467
When you straighten,

175
00:04:35,467 --> 00:04:36,907
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:37,027 --> 00:04:38,267
That's the band.

177
00:04:38,307 --> 00:04:40,697
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:40,757 --> 00:04:41,637
And you start being

179
00:04:41,637 --> 00:04:42,827
the one who says,

180
00:04:42,827 --> 00:04:43,817
you go ahead.

181
00:04:43,857 --> 00:04:45,017
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:45,207 --> 00:04:47,127
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:47,127 --> 00:04:49,437
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:49,787 --> 00:04:51,807
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:51,807 --> 00:04:52,787
around the knee.

186
00:04:52,917 --> 00:04:53,757
Worth doing,

187
00:04:53,757 --> 00:04:54,887
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:55,007 --> 00:04:56,447
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:56,447 --> 00:04:57,607
taking up room.

190
00:04:57,717 --> 00:04:59,047
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:59,047 --> 00:05:00,947
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:03,317
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:03,357 --> 00:05:04,757
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:04,757 --> 00:05:06,257
finally calms down,

195
00:05:06,257 --> 00:05:07,717
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:07,717 --> 00:05:09,207
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:09,247 --> 00:05:11,017
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:11,017 --> 00:05:12,977
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:13,127 --> 00:05:14,817
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:14,868 --> 00:05:16,388
After two years of this,

201
00:05:16,388 --> 00:05:17,958
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:18,288 --> 00:05:20,188
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:20,318 --> 00:05:22,198
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:22,548 --> 00:05:24,038
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:24,128 --> 00:05:26,528
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:26,798 --> 00:05:28,478
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:28,478 --> 00:05:32,298
kneeling pads, compression
braces, creams,

208
00:05:32,298 --> 00:05:33,908
half of Amazon really,

209
00:05:33,908 --> 00:05:35,088
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:35,088 --> 00:05:36,078
me was an hour.

211
00:05:36,238 --> 00:05:37,198
I even looked at going

212
00:05:37,198 --> 00:05:38,948
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:39,108 --> 00:05:41,108
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:41,108 --> 00:05:43,168
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:43,168 --> 00:05:44,398
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:44,738 --> 00:05:45,738
Then one night I went

217
00:05:45,738 --> 00:05:47,028
back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:47,028 --> 00:05:48,648
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:48,868 --> 00:05:50,188
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:50,188 --> 00:05:51,938
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:51,938 --> 00:05:54,528
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

222
00:05:54,528 --> 00:05:55,978
nobody could explain.

223
00:05:56,498 --> 00:05:58,418
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:58,418 --> 00:06:00,378
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:06:00,558 --> 00:06:01,838
This one device,

226
00:06:01,838 --> 00:06:03,278
and people saying

227
00:06:03,278 --> 00:06:04,608
it was the first thing

228
00:06:04,608 --> 00:06:05,958
that made a difference.

229
00:06:06,128 --> 00:06:08,048
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

230
00:06:08,048 --> 00:06:09,878
alright, here it comes,

231
00:06:09,878 --> 00:06:11,408
he's selling me something,

232
00:06:11,408 --> 00:06:13,478
let me shut that down
right now.

233
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:15,668
I'm only here because I
made myself

234
00:06:15,668 --> 00:06:17,738
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

235
00:06:17,738 --> 00:06:18,648
that if I ever found

236
00:06:18,648 --> 00:06:19,778
something that helped,

237
00:06:19,778 --> 00:06:20,768
I'd say so.

238
00:06:20,928 --> 00:06:22,428
It's called the KenRelief
Red

239
00:06:22,428 --> 00:06:23,710
Light Therapy Wrap.

240
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:25,560
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

241
00:06:25,770 --> 00:06:27,440
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

242
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:29,710
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

243
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:31,830
But I went to their
website anyway,

244
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:32,660
just to see what all

245
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:33,710
the fuss was about.

246
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:36,540
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

247
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:40,030
charge $200 a session for,
off machines

248
00:06:40,030 --> 00:06:42,360
that cost fifty thousand
dollars,

249
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,550
in a wrap

250
00:06:43,550 --> 00:06:45,620
you plug into the wall at
home.

251
00:06:45,970 --> 00:06:47,720
Two hundred and forty
lights.

252
00:06:47,810 --> 00:06:50,280
Red at 660 nanometers

253
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:53,070
and near-infrared at 850,

254
00:06:53,070 --> 00:06:55,290
run together for the
strongest effect.

255
00:06:55,430 --> 00:06:56,920
Four strength levels.

256
00:06:57,020 --> 00:06:58,840
A five to thirty minute
timer.

257
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,600
Then I saw the guarantee.

258
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:01,880
Ninety days.

259
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:03,930
Results or your money
back,

260
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:06,410
no questions, no store
credit,

261
00:07:06,410 --> 00:07:07,940
and you don't even send it
back.

262
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:11,220
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

263
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,930
days to change my mind.

264
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:14,390
There wasn't much to lose,

265
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:15,460
so I ordered it.

266
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,950
Two of them, actually.

267
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:19,300
Only the right knee was
replaced,

268
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:21,500
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

269
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:23,320
and I'd done it for two
years.

270
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,940
The left one was carrying
the difference.

271
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:26,820
When it came,

272
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:29,310
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

273
00:07:29,310 --> 00:07:30,660
because I'd been let down
too

274
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,320
many times to get excited.

275
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:34,170
What I felt was warmth.

276
00:07:34,210 --> 00:07:36,150
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

277
00:07:36,190 --> 00:07:37,850
More like it was coming
from inside

278
00:07:37,850 --> 00:07:39,700
the knee and spreading
around it.

279
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:40,840
And that was it.

280
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,380
That was the whole
experience.

281
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,750
When I took it off,

282
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:44,820
I'll be honest,

283
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:46,440
nothing dramatic had
happened.

284
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,130
And after what that video
said,

285
00:07:48,130 --> 00:07:50,250
that's exactly what I
expected.

286
00:07:50,610 --> 00:07:51,340
What was different

287
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,430
was that for the first

288
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:53,820
time in two years

289
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:55,630
I'd done something for my
knee

290
00:07:55,630 --> 00:07:56,790
instead of to it.

291
00:07:57,020 --> 00:07:57,750
Twenty minutes,

292
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:58,610
in my own chair,

293
00:07:58,610 --> 00:07:59,340
after work.

294
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:01,390
No drive, no copay.

295
00:08:01,430 --> 00:08:02,700
They say twenty minutes.

296
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:03,820
I did thirty,

297
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:04,650
twice a day,

298
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,390
lowest setting that first
week.

299
00:08:06,430 --> 00:08:07,760
I put it on the calendar.

300
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:08,570
The first week,

301
00:08:08,570 --> 00:08:09,230
I couldn't have told

302
00:08:09,230 --> 00:08:10,540
you if anything was
happening.

303
00:08:10,690 --> 00:08:11,380
I tried not to get

304
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:12,400
my hopes up.

305
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:14,130
I'd had things help for a
week

306
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:15,220
and then stop.

307
00:08:15,550 --> 00:08:16,870
But somewhere in the
second week

308
00:08:16,870 --> 00:08:17,940
I noticed I'd come down

309
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:19,750
the stairs without holding
the rail.

310
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:21,290
I hadn't decided to.

311
00:08:21,330 --> 00:08:22,440
I just did it,

312
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:25,050
then stopped halfway down
because I realized.

313
00:08:25,290 --> 00:08:27,280
By the end of the fourth
week

314
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,450
I'd slept through the
night

315
00:08:28,450 --> 00:08:29,810
four times running.

316
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,100
I stood at the counter

317
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,630
and finished making dinner

318
00:08:32,630 --> 00:08:34,160
without looking for the
stool.

319
00:08:34,290 --> 00:08:35,740
None of that is dramatic.

320
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:36,630
All of it was gone

321
00:08:36,630 --> 00:08:37,790
for two years.

322
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,690
A few weeks later my wife
asked

323
00:08:39,690 --> 00:08:40,590
if I wanted to walk

324
00:08:40,590 --> 00:08:42,210
the long way around the
block.

325
00:08:42,510 --> 00:08:43,460
And for the first time

326
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:44,150
in two years,

327
00:08:44,150 --> 00:08:45,270
I said yes.

328
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:46,990
I wanted to understand
why,

329
00:08:46,990 --> 00:08:48,310
so I read the whole thing.

330
00:08:48,830 --> 00:08:50,550
It comes down to four
steps.

331
00:08:50,590 --> 00:08:51,330
One.

332
00:08:51,570 --> 00:08:53,220
The tissue around a new
knee can

333
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:55,980
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

334
00:08:56,350 --> 00:08:56,900
Two.

335
00:08:57,250 --> 00:08:59,290
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

336
00:08:59,290 --> 00:09:00,180
so it takes up more

337
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:01,340
room than it should.

338
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:01,970
Three.

339
00:09:02,010 --> 00:09:03,780
There's only so much room
in there.

340
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:05,120
Bending compresses it.

341
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,090
Straightening pulls it
tight.

342
00:09:07,130 --> 00:09:08,600
That's the squeeze.

343
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,400
Four.

344
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,470
Red and near-infrared
light have been

345
00:09:11,470 --> 00:09:13,720
studied for calming that
inflammation,

346
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,150
so the swelling and the
pressure

347
00:09:15,150 --> 00:09:16,590
can come down with it.

348
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,510
In a randomized trial,

349
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:20,160
patients given light
therapy

350
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,770
after a knee replacement

351
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:23,290
had less pain,

352
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:26,130
less swelling and better
early movement

353
00:09:26,130 --> 00:09:27,350
than those who weren't.

354
00:09:27,390 --> 00:09:30,070
A 2025 review said the
same,

355
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:31,170
and was clear the evidence

356
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:32,200
is still limited.

357
00:09:32,450 --> 00:09:33,900
I probably sound like a
broken

358
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,020
record to my family

359
00:09:35,020 --> 00:09:36,340
and the guys on my crew.

360
00:09:36,710 --> 00:09:38,560
But after two years of
doing everything

361
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,670
I was told and getting
nowhere,

362
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:41,930
you have no idea what it's

363
00:09:41,930 --> 00:09:43,420
like to sleep through the
night,

364
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,070
say yes to the walk,

365
00:09:45,070 --> 00:09:46,590
and get my life back.

366
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:47,870
So take it from me.

367
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:49,720
Don't spend another year
waiting

368
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:50,760
for it to settle.

369
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:52,690
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

370
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:54,350
More than ten thousand
people

371
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:56,330
with pain after a knee
replacement

372
00:09:56,330 --> 00:09:57,890
have already tried this.

373
00:09:57,930 --> 00:09:59,660
Some had it worse than I
did.

374
00:09:59,850 --> 00:10:01,770
You can get the KenRelief
wrap

375
00:10:01,770 --> 00:10:03,170
from their website,

376
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:04,700
